    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Situated in a mature and highly sought-after residential development, this attractive three-bedroom semi-detached home offers an excellent opportunity for buyers seeking a prime Ballinteer address. Well maintained throughout, the property is presented in generally good condition and, while it would benefit from some modernisation, provides the perfect opportunity to create a home tailored to individual tastes. The property also benefits from off-street parking to the front and a generously sized rear garden, ideal for outdoor living or future extension potential, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nIdeally located within walking distance of Ballinteer Shopping Centre, the property enjoys easy access to a wide range of shops, cafés and everyday amenities. The area is renowned for its family-friendly atmosphere and is well served by excellent schools, parks, sporting facilities and public transport, with Marlay Park, Dundrum Town Centre and the M50 all close by. Offering a peaceful setting combined with outstanding convenience, this is an ideal home for first-time buyers, growing families or those looking to add their own personal touch.\r\n\r\nBroadford is a mature and highly regarded residential development offering a family-friendly setting with excellent local amenities. The area is served by a superb selection of primary and secondary schools, including Wesley College, Ballinteer Community School, Holy Cross School, Taney Parish Primary School and Scoil Naithí.\r\n\r\nResidents enjoy an excellent range of recreational facilities, including Meadowbrook Leisure Centre, St. Enda's Park, Ballinteer St John's GAA Club, and Grange and Stackstown Golf Clubs. SuperValu Ballinteer is just a short walk away, while Nutgrove Shopping Centre and Dundrum Town Centre can be reached within 5–7 minutes by car.\r\n\r\nMarlay Park is only a five-minute walk from the property, while Ticknock, the Dublin Mountains, Carrickmines Retail Park and the Sandyford Business District are all within a 10-minute drive. The area is well connected by Dublin Bus routes 14, 16 and S8, while the LUAS at Balally is approximately a 25 minute walk away. The nearby M50 provides convenient access to Dublin Airport and the national road network."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway\r\nUnderstairs storage.\r\n\r\nLiving Room (approx. 4.3 m x 4.0 m)\r\nBright living room with floor-to-ceiling windows, stone fireplace and hearth with gas coal-effect fire, door to:\r\n\r\nDining Room (approx. 3.7 m x 3.0 m)\r\nDoor to kitchen.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Breakfast Room (approx. 4.1 m x 2.7 m)\r\nFitted kitchen with a range of built-in cupboards and drawers, single-drainer stainless steel sink unit, plumbed for washing machine, integrated oven, hob and extractor fan, storage cupboard/larder press, and door to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\n\r\nLanding\r\nHot press with dual immersion and access to attic.\r\n\r\nBedroom One (approx. 4.4 m x 3.8 m)\r\nBuilt-in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nBedroom Two (approx. 3.8 m x 3.6 m)\r\nBuilt-in wardrobes and laminated timber flooring.\r\n\r\nBedroom Three (approx. 2.7 m x 2.5 m)\r\nLaminated timber flooring.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nWC, WHB, tiled bath with Triton shower unit.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nFront\r\nLawned front garden with mature hedging and off-street parking.\r\n\r\nRear\r\nFully walled rear garden laid to lawn with a large barna-style garden shed."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tGas-fired central heating (GFCH)\r\n•\tDouble-glazed windows\r\n•\tOff-street parking\r\n•\tApprox. 95 sq. m. / 1,022 sq. ft.\r\n•\tWithin walking distance of Ballinteer Shopping Centre\r\n•\tRegular Dublin Bus service within a short walk\r\n•\tShort drive to the M50"
      },
